Hello,
That is correct, it was removed it in the current version because we want to revisit the calculation and write a dedicated goodness-of-fit function for the next release which then correctly handles standard and Royle-Nichols occupancy models and accounts for the peculiarities of both JAGS and Nimblem But currently it it is not available since the priority was to get it back in .
You can use release 2.2.1 on GitHub which still returns the bayesian p-values.
Best regards,
Jürgen

